Cd into where raw reads are (human_gut_metagenome)

To get the md5s for the downloads on the server

Run:
-------------------------------------------------------

md5sum SAMEA*/* > checksums.md5

----------------------------------------------------


Then download the .tsv file from ENA as the expected downloads for comparison
Sort into two .txt files:

Run:
----------------------------------------------

awk '{print $1}' ~/Projects/PRJEB75460/human_gut_metagenome/checksums.md5 | sort > computed.txt

tail -n +2 ~/Projects/PRJEB75460/filereport_read_run_PRJEB75460.tsv | \
    awk -F'\t' '{split($4, a, ";"); print a[1]; print a[2]}' | sort > expected.txt

# -n +2 removes header
# TSV columns: 
# $1 = run_accession 
# $2 = study_accession 
# $3 = sample_accession 
# $4 = fastq_md5

# split($4, a, ";") separates the two checksums into: # a[1] = MD5 checksum for the first FASTQ file (R1) # a[2] = MD5 checksum for the second FASTQ file (R2)


# Compare 
# use diff to compare .txt files (downloaded and expected), any differences indicate files that havent been up or downloaded correctly, need to be checked (removed and redownloaded or removed if a fault on ZOEs side)

diff computed.txt expected.txt

